WEBVTT

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.420
Fumihiko!

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.930
Another disappearance?

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.950
People in this town keep vanishing.

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:12.480
There's a silly rumor going
around that a tengu did it.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.620
But you know, I think I heard a story once,

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.120
in which a Tamaru lord came here to
Minami-Kamiyama to hunt hawks,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.870
and a tengu appeared and told him it was
wrong to take another being's life.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.600
I see.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.370
But why would a tengu attack people?

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:33.890
In the Edo Period, there was a kid
called "Tengu Kid Torakichi."

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:37.590
Records explain how a tengu kidnapped
him and took him to the other world.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:43.070
Nationology Scholar Hirata Atsutane wrote
a book called the <i>Senkyoimon</i>,

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.780
based on his interviews with Torakichi.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.770
It's not the Edo Period anymore.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.040
Tengu. How stupid.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.600
Morning, Maya.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.350
I know!

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:57.360
Let's try and see if we can
prove there's a tengu!

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.950
I don't think you can do that
with a bug catcher's net.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.240
Maybe if the tengu's little?

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.100
A tengu!

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.290
I'm a teacher!

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.140
Sit down!

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.950
Y-Yes, sir...

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:14.790
What?

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:18.050
I was just thinking that I'm in
the same class as you again.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.520
A tengu, huh?

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.910
<i>There are all kinds of strange
rumors about the place.</i>

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:35.190
<i>Ghosts, monsters, supernatural
phenomena...</i>

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.660
<i>A while ago, someone said
they saw a tengu demon!</i>

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.670
<i>And it's almost the 21st century.</i>

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:44.980
A tengu?

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.620
The rumors are especially prevalent

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.210
around Minami-Kamiyama and Zouzan Bunker.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:55.330
So what?

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.150
"Tengu" was originally a Chinese
term meaning "Dogs of Heaven,"

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.060
that is, shooting stars.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.590
It might be a UFO or something.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.550
There's a theory that claims the beak of a

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:08.220
Karasu Tengu is actually the oxygen
mask of an astronaut.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.420
You know a lot about this.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.020
You really do like the-

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.190
What is your job?

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:18.650
Find the Key of Nostradamus
and stop the prophecy.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.870
Then what if the tengu are actually an

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:23.470
advance scouting team for
the aliens or something?

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:27.720
I get it... They might lead
us to the key somehow!

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.790
Even if it seems impossible,

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.370
don't just deny the possibility
without thinking!

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.780
If something seems strange, investigate,

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.960
and if you think it needs it,
photograph it with your phone.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.670
Got it?

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.560
Yes.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.880
And no matter what the tengu are,

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.640
they may have killed my father.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.400
Abe-sensei?

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.450
What is it?

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.470
Your tie is crooked.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:03.570
Oh, right.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:06.320
And do something about the
creases in your trousers.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.200
A teacher must be an example
to the students.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.900
Messy clothes are the sign of a messy soul.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.070
By the way...

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:19.290
You seem to be visiting the principal's
office quite often.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.420
Is there something you need from her?

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.770
Um...

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:28.760
That hair style really fits you.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.750
What's wrong?

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.720
That's the first time...

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.610
It's the first time someone's
actually praised my hair.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:49.490
The students call them "the two dumpling
brothers" after a song...

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:51.990
I love you.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.990
Abe-sensei...

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.170
I hook up with her.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:38.500
Ow...

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.340
Abe-san...

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.110
Yes?

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:48.160
Make sure you separate out
your garbage properly.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.360
Did you read the pamphlet?

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:52.510
Flammable garbage is Monday,
Wednesday, and Friday.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:53.710
Separated garbage is...

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:55.890
Yes, I understand.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.700
I'll be careful!

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.040
Geez, what the hell is wrong
with everybody?

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:31.550
The young boy with psychic powers

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.500
Behold!

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.610
The spoon is bent!

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:39.890
Bunmei-kun's so awesome!

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.860
That was Uchida Bunmei,
the spoon-bender!

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.610
Bunmei-kun is so cute!

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:55.910
It's not Bunmei. It's Fumiaki-chan!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.000
But this recording was great.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:08.040
I made your favorite today.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:09.750
Curry!

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:13.220
Thanks!

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:19.600
Good times back then.

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.680
I really want to go back...

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.790
Wait, I am back!

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:46.480
Yes, this is the Uchida residence.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.120
Who is this?

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:51.320
U-Uh...

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:55.200
Fumiaki-chan! Don't put
so much sauce on it!

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.510
Okay!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.070
I'm sorry.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.630
Who is this?

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:22.510
Welcome.

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:25.330
Landlord?

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:30.380
Oh, you meant my little sister, Tanoko?

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:33.880
Yes... I think.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.180
I shouldn't have come here.

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:44.600
Curry...

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.020
Here you go. Just a second.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.260
Here you are!

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.720
It's taken way too long...

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.060
Just my type.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.820
Just my type.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:42.860
Do you like curry that much?

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:47.200
Yes. I could eat it every day.

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:53.130
Look over here!

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:54.750
Bunmei-chan!

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.520
Bend a spoon!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:02.640
Everyone loved me just 'cause
I could bend a spoon.

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:05.930
But once I couldn't...

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:10.970
Um, may I get some chopsticks?

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.650
You eat curry with chopsticks?

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:16.440
You're so cute Bunmei-kun!

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:24.870
Only my mom called me "Fumiaki."

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.330
Fumiaki-chan's so cute.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.940
Is something wrong?

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.130
What did you just say?

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:39.040
Is something wrong?

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.430
No, before that.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:45.890
Um... You eat curry with chopsticks?

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.720
Not that far back.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.510
What did I say?

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:52.800
I know!

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:55.150
Fumiaki-chan's so cute!

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.820
Fumiaki-chan...

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:04.240
She's the first person, besides
my mom, to call me that.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:10.830
Because Fumiaki-chan is cute!

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.070
Mikaze!

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:16.390
Stop making small talk and come help!

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:17.460
Right!

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.490
I'll be right there!

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:23.710
We're not busy at all, though.

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:34.390
Mikaze-san, huh?

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:36.230
That's a nice name.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:43.780
A tengu?

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.240
No way.

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:54.340
Where's Kozue?

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:55.960
Who knows.

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.170
Maybe she went to look for a tengu.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.230
Maybe she went to train
her spiritual powers.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:01.090
Spiritual powers?

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:04.420
Sometimes she'll stand under a waterfall
or live at a temple for a while.

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:08.430
Wow, she goes all out.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:17.400
Because Fumiaki-chan is cute!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.780
Bunmei!

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:21.480
Bunmei!

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.610
How's the investigation going?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:26.570
The investigation?

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:28.820
Of the tengu.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:32.660
The tengu... Yeah, the tengu.

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:34.840
Fine.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:36.630
All good.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:39.210
Come to me! Come to me!

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:42.210
JK, what are you looking for?

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.470
A tengu. For my class on Japanese youkai.

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:47.680
You think there is one?

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.820
Hell if I know.

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:53.510
But if there is, then my rods will find it.

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:58.190
There's a tengu. No doubt about it.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.980
I got it. I got it.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:03.480
Good evening.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:10.550
You're a new teacher at Waldstein
Academy, aren't you?

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:12.910
I am. How'd you know?

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:15.050
It's a small town.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:17.290
I'll get the chopsticks.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:21.080
Hi!

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:30.050
What's this?

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:31.960
A little bonus.

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:33.580
Thank you.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:38.700
Didn't you say you were busy with work
and hadn't had time to see the town?

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:39.900
Yeah.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.650
Want me to show you around tomorrow?

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.020
Really?

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:47.160
I've got free time.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.530
It's a promise.

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:51.530
Yes, of course.

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:02.670
Man, this station is ancient.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:05.590
It's gotta be as old as my grandfather.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:18.110
Abe-sensei, sorry to keep you waiting.

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:20.430
I-Is this yours?

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:22.690
Yes. Come on, get in.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:25.470
Wow!

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:28.230
I've wanted a car like this since I was a kid!

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:31.040
Please put your seat belt on.

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.150
You do it like this.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.540
It's not working...

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.090
It's done.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.520
I guess we could start with
the Sanada Mansion.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:53.580
And then Matsushiro Castle...

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:57.080
Or maybe Zouzan Bunker?

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.220
I'll leave it to you.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:15:59.520
Okay!

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:02.640
You can show me-

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:18.190
Sanada Mansion

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:18.200
This is the Sanada Mansion.

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:24.270
The 9th lord of this province, Sanada
Yukinori, built this for his mother.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.590
Shall we go to the next spot?

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:36.430
This is the Sanada Museum.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.760
All kinds of artifacts from the
Sanada family's history are housed here.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:42.260
I brought you a map of Matsushiro.

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:44.910
Thanks for taking the trouble
on your day off.

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:47.610
Not at all. By the way, what
will you be using this for?

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:50.020
Something that you don't
need to know about.

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:04.230
So that's all the places in Matsushiro where
people have been kidnapped...

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:07.290
Zouzan Bunker.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:11.990
It's a ten kilometer
underground bunker.

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:15.300
They planned to move Army HQ,
as well as most of the government,

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.340
here during the last days of the war.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:20.240
They were planning to move
the emperor, too.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:24.760
It must've been quite a power spot.

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:28.350
These is the ruins of Matsushiro Castle.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:34.740
Isn't that Matsushiro Station?

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.400
It is.

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:39.470
Did we have to come by car then?

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:43.910
You didn't want to drive with me?

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:46.220
No, that's not it!

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:47.420
Of course I did!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.190
Good. I'm glad.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.670
Then let's go to the next place.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.840
This oyaki's good.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:59.830
What was yours?

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:00.970
Eggplant miso.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:03.300
Leaf mustard is great.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:04.570
Try some?

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:07.140
But...

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:09.900
Don't worry about it.

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:14.060
An indirect kiss!

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:19.460
Do you like it?

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:22.790
It's a snack now,

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:25.700
but until a while ago, this was one
of the few things available to eat.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.120
Really?

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:29.840
You can't get much rice
out here, you know?

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.940
So they would knead wheat flour,

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:35.590
put some pickled vegetables in it,
and bake it in the ashes of their hearth.

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.670
Real oyaki's covered with ash.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:52.360
Next is Zouzan Bunker.

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:54.320
Right.

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:57.280
Don't talk while you eat.

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:03.180
You're pretty funny.

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:04.490
You think?

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:14.090
This was made over sixty years ago, huh?

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:16.800
Hey, don't be silly.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.510
You're a history teacher, right?

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:21.520
The war ended fifty-four years ago.

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:24.350
You're right.

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:27.970
I'd be so embarrassed in
front of my students.

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:33.400
Is there no one here?

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.230
I guess not.

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:38.900
Normally, there are lots of tourists.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.470
I'm sorry.

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:44.840
I'm fine.

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:46.370
Be careful.

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.000
The ground's rough here.

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:54.550
Usually, there are other people
here, and it's not scary.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:56.710
But when we're alone...

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.300
It's all right.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.130
I'm with you.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:06.010
My whole body's turned into an arm!

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:19.280
After all the yelling I did, what the
hell is he doing slacking off?

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:29.080
What is this?

00:20:38.810 --> 00:20:40.210
I'm sorry.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:41.740
It's fine.

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:45.810
But you just started crying...
I was surprised.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:49.430
I just can't take it, looking at that.

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:52.620
You mean those paper cranes?

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:55.340
What are those?

00:20:55.340 --> 00:20:57.030
There were so many...

00:20:58.180 --> 00:21:01.360
They're for the dead.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:05.140
Zouzan Bunker was built as fast as possible.

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:08.320
They pushed the workers
beyond their limits.

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:12.750
So many people died there.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:16.560
Dying so deep beneath the ground...

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:20.000
When I think of how painful
it must've been...

00:21:38.590 --> 00:21:43.960
She must be a kind girl to cry for people who
died when her grandfather was alive.

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:51.520
A brief and gentle gust of wind
blows through my heart,

00:23:51.520 --> 00:23:53.080
as I struggle with my terrible mission.

00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:54.060
"Terrible?"

00:23:54.060 --> 00:23:55.750
You're not doing anything!

00:23:55.750 --> 00:23:56.600
Sorry, sorry!

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:57.650
Oh, hey. A butterfly!

00:23:57.650 --> 00:23:59.470
That's not a butterfly, it's...

00:23:59.470 --> 00:24:00.080
It's...

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:01.330
A moth-

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:03.580
You mean the one that built
a cocoon on Tokyo Tower?

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:04.570
No!

00:24:04.570 --> 00:24:07.690
But I'm so embarrassed I can't say it!

00:24:07.690 --> 00:24:10.050
